    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CO OUR PATRONS\nPARTIES \u0026 DINNERS with specially prepared menus may be\narranged with our maitre d'hotel.\nKindly ask the head waiter for souvenir menus ready for mailing.\nTHE ENTERTAINMENT AND INFORMATION DESKS are lo-\ncated in the lobby, where arrangements may be made for sports\nactivities and motor tours.\nTHE QUIET RESTFUL SIXTH FLOOR SUN LOUNGE:\nHigh\nabove the street, a rare view of the Broad Pacific and the Beau-\ntiful Koolau Mountain Range may be had.\nTHE WAIALAE GOLF COURSE offers you the finest 18-hole\ngolf links in the Territory. Completely equipped clubhouse. Ted\nBenedict, Professional. Green fees $2.00 on Mondays, Tuesdays,\nThursdays and Fridays and $2.50 on Wednesdays, Saturdays,\nSundays and Holidays.\nMonthly rates quoted.\nDinner-dance\nevery Tuesday and Friday.\nSpecial parties arranged.\nTENNIS: The Royal Hawaiian Hotel Courts are available to\nguests of the Moana\nHotel. Tennis Instruction by Phil Bagby,\nProfessional. Courts may be reserved and appointments for in-\nstruction made through the front office.\nA VISIT to the pineapple cannery is interesting.\nPlease see\nthe clerk at the front desk.\nA CRATE OF FRESH HAWAIIAN PINEAPPLES can be\nshipped by refrigerated express anywhere in the mainland. In-\nformation at the front office.\nEVENTS OF THE DAY\nHAWAIIAN CONCERT IN DINING ROOM\nBy Al Perry's Surf-riders.\n... 7:15 P.M.\nMOANA HOTEL\nLUNCHEON\nPoi Cocktail, Chef's Special\nPapaia Health Juice\nMarinated Sprats\nPickled Pig's Feet\nGreen Onions \u0026 Radishes\nSpiced Pineapple\nPineapple Juice\nSalad Russe\nConsomme Madrilene\nCream of Chicken a la Reine\nJellied Beef, Chicken or Tomato Broth\nFrench Onion Soup au Gratin\nFISH\nSteamed Finnan Haddie, Parsley Potatoes\nENTREES\nHam \u0026 Eggs, Country Style\nChicken Chop Suey, Moana Special\nFresh Vegetable Plate with Lamb Chop\nCoconut Waffle, Little Pig Sausages, Ono Syrup\nCold Dutch Luncheon Plate\nBroiled Top Sirloin Steak, Tyrolienne\nVEGETABLE\nButtered Cabbage\nFried Egg-plant\nSpinach with Hard Boiled Egg\nGreen Beans Saute\nBoiled Rice\nWainaku Lehua Poi\nPotatoes - Baked, Hashed Brown, Mashed or New Boiled\nCOLD BUFFET\nAssorted Cold Cuts\nCorned Beef\nSugar Cured Ham\nHead Cheese\nSpring Lamb, Mint Jelly\nSmoked Beef Tongue\nPrime Ribs of Beef\nImported Salami\nBismark Herring\nGalantine of Capon\nSALAD\nTropical Fruit\nVegetable Mayonnaise\nDESSERT\nDeepdish Fresh Apple Pie\nCompote of Preserved Fruit\nPeach \u0026 Vermicelli Pudding\nOrange Jello\nPetit Fours\nVanilla Cup Custard\nFrench Vanilla, Chocolate or Coconut Ice Cream\nApples\nCHEESE\nAmerican, Cottage, Roquefort, Swiss, Monterey or Philadelphia Cream\nButtermilk\nSanka Coffee \u0026 Ovaltine\nPineapple Juice Frappee\nDishes ordered that are not on the Menu will be charged extra.\nRoom Service 25\ncents each person.\nBreakfast 7 to 10\nLuncheon 12 to 2\nDinner 6 to 8.\nHonolulu, Hawaii, U.S. A.\nSunday, December 26th, 1937",
      "A HONOLULU LEI VENDER",
      "ROYAL\nHAWAllAN HOTEL\nMOANA HOTEL\nAL WAIALAE GOLF CLUB I!\nSEASIDE HOTEL\nTHE TERRITORIAL HOTEL CO., LTD.-HONOLULU, HAWAII"
    ],
